Inclusion Criteria:

          -  Patients age older than 18 years (including 18 years old);

          -  The primary lesion is located in the upper or middle third of the stomach, including
             Siewert II type and Siewert III type adenocarcinoma of the esophagogastric junction;

          -  Pathologically confirmed primary gastric adenocarcinoma by endoscopic biopsy
             (including papillary, tubular, mucinous, signet ring cell and poorly differentiated
